 for 24- and 48-h. Note that vitamin-E isomers, particularly tocotrienols, selectively affect the viability of the prostate cancer cells at a different degree, but do not have a significant effect on the non-tumorigenic prostate epithelial cells. PC-3 is more responsive to vitamin-E isomers compared with LNCaP. (B) LNCaP and PC-3 growth rate in the presence of <italic>&#x003b3;</italic>-T3 at IC<sub>50</sub>. The IC<sub>50</sub> dose levels correspond to that in <xref rid="tbl1" ref-type="table">Table 1A</xref>. For <italic>&#x003b1;</italic>-T3, 100&#x02009;<italic>&#x003bc;</italic><sc>M</sc> was used. UD indicates undetermined IC<sub>50</sub>.</p></fn></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap></floats-wrap></article>